; MAC-HYG-3a: a renamed binder renders under its original spelling.
; `(m 5)` expands `(let ((tmpvar x)) ...)` with `tmpvar` renamed to
; `tmpvar.0`, which no source can spell. The typo `tmpvarr` suggests
; `tmpvar`, not `tmpvar.0`, and carries no `~>` (MAC-TOOL-5: the fix
; is disarmed inside an expansion). The hand-written pair keeps its
; `~>"count"`.
(macro (m x) (let ((tmpvar x)) (+ tmpvarr 1)))
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (+ (m 5) (let ((count 1)) (+ cound 1))))
